      "side": 1,
      "message": "One thought to minimize the boilerplate: we could add a RAII-style private helper that handles budget management, something like\n\n```\n   class ScopedAllocBudget {\n       SkCodec* fCodec;\n     public:\n       ScopedAllocBudget(SkCodec* codec, Options* options)\n         : fCodec(codec) {\n           SkASSERT(codec-\u003efAllocBudget \u003d\u003d SIZE_MAX); // hopefully we\u0027re not nesting\n           codec-\u003efAllocBudget \u003d (options \u0026\u0026 options-\u003efMaxDecodeMemory)\n                   ? options-\u003efMaxDecodeMemory : SIZE_MAX;\n       }\n       ~ScopedAllocBudget() {\n           fCodec-\u003efAllocBudget \u003d SIZE_MAX;\n       }\n   }\n```\n\nThen we only need to add `ScopedAllocBudget sab(this, options);` to the entry points.",
      "revId": "159158fb34fc3ba480cf20e24b5fb454f8a90899",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
